{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VvNr8R37RLmzGRmyucKf9G","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t## Problem\n2\t\n3\tClass: fix\n4\t\n5\tThe reviews of the 2026-10-14 wave passed with four findings, none blocking, each a few lines. They are one item because each is small and they share a wave.\n6\t\n7\t1. #339's rejection test proves the claim's `at` equals the version's `at`, not that the clock is read once. A call count on `now_iso` for one `plan claims` write proves the stronger claim (the product already reads once; the test is what is missing).\n8\t2. `store.put`'s own stamp, when the caller passes no `at`, has no regression test.\n9\t3. #351's review read the gate as judging criterion kinds before the exit-code contract. The spec's own push found the contract is already judged first: a structural criterion that exits 1 on the tree and 2 on the stub is refused \"criterion could not check (exit 2)\" on main today. The finding needs no logic; its test pins the order.\n10\t4. `attavo/types.py` types an intervention's `class` as `str`; the schema is the enum `amend`, `launch`, `transport`. A TypedDict for an intervention carries it as a `Literal`, and the mirror test reads enums against literals.\n11\t\n12\tThe stub is thin: the four tests, one per finding, in their files; the one that needs logic (4) is red on the stub. The build writes the logic.\n13\t\n14\tRetires: four gaps a second reader found that the first reader's tests did not cover.\n15\t\n16\t## Claims\n17\t\n18\t- attavo/spec.py\n19\t- attavo/types.py\n20\t- tests/test_plan.py\n21\t- tests/test_store.py\n22\t- tests/test_spec_gate.py\n23\t- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n24\t\n25\t## Criteria\n26\t\n27\t- [structural] the-rejection-tests-exist.sh: the four tests exist, one per finding, in tests/test_plan.py, tests/test_store.py, tests/test_spec_gate.py and tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n28\t- [behavioural] the-intervention-class-type-is-the-schemas-enum.sh: a TypedDict in attavo.types for an intervention types class as the Literal of the schema's enum\n29\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"98798923-8d1f-4f23-9171-7d9c27508aed","uuid":"dcd29188-ad60-431e-892a-fce21f81ce3e","timestamp":"2026-10-15T15:11:36.107Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-360/attest/specs/360/spec.md","content":"## Problem\n\nClass: fix\n\nThe reviews of the 2026-10-14 wave passed with four findings, none blocking, each a few lines. They are one item because each is small and they share a wave.\n\n1. #339's rejection test proves the claim's `at` equals the version's `at`, not that the clock is read once. A call count on `now_iso` for one `plan claims` write proves the stronger claim (the product already reads once; the test is what is missing).\n2. `store.put`'s own stamp, when the caller passes no `at`, has no regression test.\n3. #351's review read the gate as judging criterion kinds before the exit-code contract. The spec's own push found the contract is already judged first: a structural criterion that exits 1 on the tree and 2 on the stub is refused \"criterion could not check (exit 2)\" on main today. The finding needs no logic; its test pins the order.\n4. `attavo/types.py` types an intervention's `class` as `str`; the schema is the enum `amend`, `launch`, `transport`. A TypedDict for an intervention carries it as a `Literal`, and the mirror test reads enums against literals.\n\nThe stub is thin: the four tests, one per finding, in their files; the one that needs logic (4) is red on the stub. The build writes the logic.\n\nRetires: four gaps a second reader found that the first reader's tests did not cover.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/spec.py\n- attavo/types.py\n- tests/test_plan.py\n- tests/test_store.py\n- tests/test_spec_gate.py\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- [structural] the-rejection-tests-exist.sh: the four tests exist, one per finding, in tests/test_plan.py, tests/test_store.py, tests/test_spec_gate.py and tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n- [behavioural] the-intervention-class-type-is-the-schemas-enum.sh: a TypedDict in attavo.types for an intervention types class as the Literal of the schema's enum\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VvNr8R37RLmzGRmyucKf9G","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
